@*
    The ascension perks, which are what an empire spends its ascension on.

    Forty-nine of them in a handful of paths, and the paths are the point: taking the first perk of
    one mostly settles the rest. The two conditions the game states are read as one list, for the
    reason the civics give - hiding a perk and blocking it are two ways of refusing the same reader.

    The second address is one entry of the shelf, as on every other page here.
*@

